Osiris runtime hook — boot the local stack from the Electron main process
========================================================================

Injects a call to `runtime/osiris-main.mjs` into VSCodium's compiled main entry,
just after the Electron `app` is ready and before the first window opens.

`scripts/apply-branding.mjs` runs `git apply --3way` for every `patches/*.patch`
and tolerates a patch that no longer applies (it warns and skips), so an upstream
bump never hard-fails branding — re-roll this hunk against the new tag.

The anchor below (`app.once('ready', ...)` in `src/vs/code/electron-main/app.ts`)
matches recent VSCodium tags. If it drifts, re-generate:

    cd apps/osiris-desktop/.build/vscode
    # add the `import('../../../runtime/osiris-main.mjs')` block after `app` is ready
    git diff > ../../patches/0002-osiris-runtime-hook.patch

--- a/src/vs/code/electron-main/main.ts
+++ b/src/vs/code/electron-main/main.ts
@@ -1,6 +1,17 @@
